# Staged by fisher-4yn.1 on 2026-11-25 for a search that makes cutoffs.
# Successor of uci/go-nodes.uci (fisher-5sg.5, 2026-11-25), whose sources stand:
# April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/,
# fisher-8ie, fisher-r6y D20, D24, D28 and D41, fisher-5sg decisions 2–6 and 10.
# Perft: expectations/perft.epd. Full info spelling: Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d),
# as cited in expectations/README.md. See README.md beside this session.
#
# Every node total at depth 2 or more reads {nodes}, as in uci/, except the
# starting position at depth 2. The startpos limits 439 and 440 change, the
# 3137 case is dropped and the 3138 case accepts further depths.
#
# 439 and 440 become 78 and 79 (fisher-4yn, "Nodes" and "Expected sessions").
# From the starting position, depth 1 enters the 20 root moves. Depth 2
# enters 59 nodes: every root move has 20 replies and no capture is possible
# within two plies, so every position two plies in has material 0. The
# first root move costs 1 + 20 nodes and sets the root's score to cp 0.
# Each of the other 19 costs 1 + 1, because its first reply already scores
# cp 0, which proves the root move no better than the first: a cutoff. The
# count does not depend on the order of moves. Total 20 + 59 = 79. A limit
# of 78 interrupts depth 2 before its last node; 79 lets it finish. A search
# without cutoffs enters 440 and fails the 79 case.
#
# The depth-5 boundary of the forced position (3137 and 3138) has no
# total a search with cutoffs must reach: at depths 3 to 5 its count depends
# on the order of moves. The 3137 case is dropped. The 3138 case stays, because
# a search with cutoffs plays a subset of the moves the search without
# cutoffs plays at each depth (Knuth and Moore, "An analysis of alpha-beta
# pruning", Artificial Intelligence 6, 1975), so its total through depth 5 is
# at most 3138 and depth 5 must finish. Deeper depths may also finish; the
# repeated record accepts them. bestmove stays h8g8, the only legal move.
> position startpos
> go nodes 0
< bestmove {legal}

> go nodes 19
< bestmove {legal}

> go nodes 20
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

> go nodes 21
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

# One node short of depth 2 (fisher-4yn: 439 becomes 78).
> go nodes 78
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

# The exact cumulative limit (fisher-4yn: 440 becomes 79).
> go nodes 79
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 79 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# The only legal move pins the zero-limit answer (D20).
> go nodes 0
< bestmove h8g8

# A limit of 3138 finishes at least depth 5 (Knuth and Moore 1975, above).
> go nodes 3138
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< info depth 5 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
<* info depth {depth} multipv 1 score {score} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove h8g8

# The sole node of depth 1 uses the entire limit. Hold the move (decision 5).
> go infinite nodes 1
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
> isready
< readyok
# Rule 8. Reject both commands and keep the original position.
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
< info string {message:position rejected: waiting for stop}
> go nodes 1
< info string {message:go rejected: waiting for stop}
> stop
# D24. The following go uses the retained position.
> go nodes 0
< bestmove h8g8
< bestmove h8g8
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go nodes 0
< bestmove h8h7

# The terminal response precedes the zero limit.
> position fen 7k/6Q1/5K2/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go nodes 0
< info depth 0 score mate 0
< bestmove 0000

> quit
! exit
